--- gate 4: in-tree specification statements on the lock bits ---
  docs/CaliptraHardwareSpecification.md: KV entry control field table
    2459:| Lock wr\[0\]              | core_only_rst_b   | Setting the lock wr field prevents the entry from being written by the microcontroller. Keys are always locked. After a lock is set, it cannot be reset until cptra_rst_b is de-asserted.               |
    2460:| Lock use\[1\]             | core_only_rst_b   | Setting the lock use field prevents the entry from being used in any cryptographic blocks. After the lock is set, it cannot be reset until cptra_rst_b is de-asserted.                                  |
  src/keyvault/config/keyvault.md: who sets the locks
    209:- **KV22 (HEK)**: **locked for writes until warm reset** (ROM requirement).
    210:- **KV16 (MDK)**: **locked for writes until warm reset** (ROM requirement).
    225:- Caliptra ROM shall lock **KV22** for writes immediately it has derived the **HEK** into that slot.
